{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow unsponsored job changes after 5 years for Skilled Workers on 10-year ILR",
        "additional_details": "The proposal for Earned Settlement extends the path to ILR from 5 to 10 years for many skilled workers. We call for: an unsponsored Bridge Route after 5 continuous sponsored years; the waiving of certificate fees, Immigration Skills Charge and sponsor tie-in for years 6\u201310; independent extensions and all bridge-route residence to be counted towards ILR. We believe this would provide fair transitional protection for all Skilled Workers already in the UK.",
        "background": "Introduce an un-sponsored, open-work visa for existing Skilled Worker visa holders who complete 5 years under tied sponsorship. This would allow workers on the proposed 10-year Earned Settlement pathway to switch employers and extend visas independently for Years 6 to 10 to reach ILR.",
